From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Date: Sun, 6 Sep 2026 20:15:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] WebPageBlink: let an explicit window.open type win over the
 inherited one

The exhibition (dock) mode change made a child window inherit the type
its parent was actually created with, so a docked "noWindow" app's
window.open carries the dock type instead of reverting to a card. That
inheritance also fired when the window.open attributes named a type of
their own: a legacy dashboard ({"window":"dashboard"} in the attributes,
mapped to a floating window) or popup alert opened by an application
whose parent has a real type got the parent's type instead.

com.palm.systemui is exactly such an application - its main window is
system_ui - so every legacy dashboard it opened (USB drive, sync, the
new captive portal one) came up as _WEBOS_WINDOW_TYPE_SYSTEM_UI, which
the shell never lists in the notification area: the dashboard existed
but was never seen. Verified on sargo through WAM's window property
log.

Only inherit the parent's type when the attributes did not ask for one;
dock mode children open plain windows and keep the inherited type.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [LuneOS specific]
---
 src/platform/webengine/web_page_blink.cc | 13 ++++++++++---
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

--- a/src/platform/webengine/web_page_blink.cc
+++ b/src/platform/webengine/web_page_blink.cc
@@ -1403,11 +1403,18 @@
   // applications are typically "noWindow": true, so the window the user
   // actually sees is this one, and it has to carry the dock type too rather
   // than reverting to a card.
+  //
+  // A type named explicitly in the window.open attributes wins over both: a
+  // dashboard or popup alert asks for its type on purpose, and inheriting
+  // instead turned com.palm.systemui's dashboards (a system_ui application)
+  // into system_ui windows the shell never lists in the notification area.
   std::string child_win_type =
       webAppMgr->WindowTypeFromString(new_app_desc->DefaultWindowType());
-  WebAppBase *parentApp = webAppMgr->FindAppById(app_id_);
-  if (parentApp && !parentApp->WindowType().empty())
-    child_win_type = parentApp->WindowType();
+  if (window_attributes["window"].asString().empty()) {
+    WebAppBase *parentApp = webAppMgr->FindAppById(app_id_);
+    if (parentApp && !parentApp->WindowType().empty())
+      child_win_type = parentApp->WindowType();
+  }
 
   WebAppBase *newWebApp = webAppMgr->CreateWindowForAppPage(child_win_type,
                                     std::move(new_app_desc), "{}", app_id_, newPage);
